# Cargo.lock is tracked because Cyberterm is an executable.

### Universal ###
# Common files that should be ignored in all projects

# Logs
*.log
# Temporary files
*.tmp
*~

*.bak
# Environment files (containing secrets, API keys, credentials)
.env
*.env
.env.*

# Local configuration that shouldn't be shared
*.local

# Rust
# rust specific files

# Contains all compiled files, build artifacts, and executables
/target/
debug/
target/debug/
target/release/

# Compilation/Backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# Logs generated by rustc when it crashes (Internal Compiler Errors)
rustc-ice-*.txt

# Mutation testing data generated by cargo-mutants
***.mutants

# Text Editors
# Kate
# Swap Files #
.*.kate-swp
.swp.*

# Intellij
# Covers JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, RubyMine, PhpStorm, AppCode, PyCharm, CLion, Android Studio, WebStorm and Rider
# Reference: https://intellij-support.jetbrains.com/hc/en-us/articles/206544839

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/

### Vscode ###
# Visual Studio Code editor settings and workspace files

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json

!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/*.code-snippets
.history/
*.vsix
.ionide

.vs/
*.code-workspace
.vscode-test
.vscodeignore
.vscode/chrome

.vscode-server/
.vscode/sftp.json
.vscode/tags
.devcontainer/

